{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1470917-let-s-talk-the-limits-of-nova-science","id":1470917,"title":"Let's talk the Limits of Nova science.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-20T01:23:02-08:00","id":1470917,"title":"Let's talk the Limits of Nova science.","content":"I may have done something like this earlier, but looking at the rules--impoprobably by around the middle of the nova era, we're going to start seeing a number of nova engineers with Mega-intelligence 5 or higher. B y the end of the nova age, mental scale 9 novas aren't impossible, and that's sitting at &quot;intelligence that makes humans look fungal.&quot; So what are the limits? I'm going to list some projects and see what people think their limits would be. <br /> <br /> 1. Initiate an eruption in someone who already has the potential for an eruption. <br /> <br /> 2. Create interstellar range gateways or FTL ships.<br /> <br /> 3. nanotech enhancements for baseline humans, granting moderate levels of super powers.<br /> <br /> 4. Infusing normal baselines with nova potential, or alternately, creating genetic organisms that also have nova traits (because what's better than a fire-breathing dragon? A dragon firing quantum bolts out of its eyes.). <br /> <br /> 4. Nanotech construction &quot;seeds&quot; that let you toss one onto the ground and watch as it grows a structure.<br /> <br /> For the start, we can assume that these are all qtech, and then go to what it would take to make them nova tech or even core tech.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T02:46:15-08:00","id":1470920,"title":"","content":"Going by the rules doing most of that wouldn't be hard for a nova apart from the eruption and nova potential stuff and that's because allowing that in story is a bit iffy. The rest of it though I don't think they would need super high mega intellect only time and resources plus making it Nova or core tech is covered by the shifting paradigm rules in aberrant book. I imagine by the middle of the nova era a bunch of stuff like this or a similar scale has been done but kept secret because the novas who did it are also smart enough to realise that the tech is too dangerous or easily abused by certain factions or baselines in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-20T04:19:58-08:00","id":1470923,"title":"","content":"All the list is not only doable, but it was done at some point before 2028.<br /> <br /> 1. N-Day is essentially this, but on global scale.<br /> 2. Warp (for gateway or ship) or teleport (for ship)<br /> 3. Must be Nova Tech, to be able to be used by baseline. Could be chemical, like mite, or cybernetics, or Nanotech, it\u2019s about the result, not the way it works.<br /> 4. This one is not hard, but it may be tricky. Quantum Construct would make it last forever as long the seed is active, so you could make one seed that constructs AND colapses back, or Trnasmutation to transforma the place into the material. First point is easy and fast, second takes many successes, but durable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T11:07:19-08:00","id":1471017,"title":"","content":"In terms of the <i>potential</i> limits of Nova science, it can do anything except things disallowed by Nova powers. So, no Telepathy or Clairsentience stuff and presumably no luck/probability/dimension-traveling stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T12:05:40-08:00","id":1471024,"title":"","content":"Though as Anima shows, that's actually a fairly blurry line: Glass is, apparently, novatech; but it lets you mess with someone's memories, which is something I'd normally associate with Telepathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T12:43:17-08:00","id":1471029,"title":"","content":"Actually I think it says novas can do stuff which mimics the effects of telepathy and clairsentience to an extent which is covered in the aberrant rule book. As for dimension traveling and other stuff since novas can affect space and time with their powers I don't see why they can't travel to other dimensions or through time, I would just probably make it so you need quantum 6+ or something (For the actual quantum power not making q-tech etc). One thing I didn't get was how psiads/psions etc can develop quantakinesis but the opposite isn't possible or mentioned.<br /> <br /> I think when it comes what novas can make tech or science wise they can pretty much make it so anything given enough time with the only constraints being story reasons. I personally would need a compelling reason why a nova can't make something other than its on its psionic stuff or novas don't have those powers because if you look at it from a baseline perspective a human can't fly to the moon or split a atom but they can make technology that can do those things.<br /> <br /> On a sidenote I disliked the whole novas can't do telepathy etc so if a player can give me a good reason I allow them to have those powers. I liked the whole novas can do anything in 1E but have do deal taint so I just kept the concept for 2E, I view it as novas dealing with transcendence is the downside to having unlimited potential.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the mini rant, it's just my personal opinion which your free to disagree with it just seems that there a few random things that have been thrown into the rules just to nerf or be novas kryptonite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T13:40:55-08:00","id":1471030,"title":"","content":"The official reasoning is that you don't want Novas trampling all over psiads and psions in the bigger picture. That said, I know for a fact that there are several Nexus authors who are chomping at the bit to produce a supplement that enables you to do the forbidden powers in Aberrant. They're just waiting for permission to make aberrant supplements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-21-2021, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T13:47:52-08:00","id":1471033,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the Mega Social Mega Edges work much like Telepathy in many ways, and the only thing missing to have a complete Telepathy is the capacity of projecting your thoughts in other people mind, what can be created with a simple Mega Edge like:<br /> <br /> Projecting Presence (**)<br /> Requisite: Mega Presence *<br /> You can communicate what you want by simply crossing your eyes with the target. Long or complex ideas may require more than a few seconds, as would to explain an idea. This Mega Edge, combined with Telecommunication allow Nova to project their thoughts to the mind of anyone, not only other Novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 12-21-2021, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T14:04:55-08:00","id":1471034,"title":"","content":"Indeed, I would expect the Nexus supplement in question to primarily consist of examples of how to stat up the equivalent of various Psi Aptitudes in terms of Aberrant powers, with maybe one or two boxes introducing new powers to fill in the holes. <br /> <br /> That, and something about how to set up an honest to goodness psiad using the rules in Aberrant, instead of the current insistence that you purchase \u00c6on and \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion if you want to play a psiad in any era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-21-2021, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T14:58:25-08:00","id":1471037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1470917-let-s-talk-the-limits-of-nova-science?p=1471017#post1471017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of the <i>potential</i> limits of Nova science, it can do anything except things disallowed by Nova powers. So, no Telepathy or Clairsentience stuff and presumably no luck/probability/dimension-traveling stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the biggest roadblock to a dimension-traveling nova is the fact that most of the powers that they'd use for such an effort are described as operating on &quot;quantum entanglement&quot;, and it is difficult to apply that explanation to alternate dimensions that don't normally interact. I'd rule that the nova would have to first perceive an alternate dimension via a dimensional flux event or journey to a Strange Place in order to target whatever dimension is on the far side of the event. So if you want to run a Sliders campaign, have one character take Detect (dimensional flux) and a custom Mega-Edge that lowers the difficulty of targeting previously detected dimensions by their Mega-Cunning (to a minimum of the power's base Difficulty), then have them learn Remote Perception and Warp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T15:01:11-08:00","id":1471038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1470917-let-s-talk-the-limits-of-nova-science?p=1471034#post1471034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, and something about how to set up an honest to goodness psiad using the rules in Aberrant, instead of the current insistence that you purchase \u00c6on and \u00c6on \u00c6xpansion if you want to play a psiad in any era.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your ideas. I honestly like the idea of Psiads working in a different way from Psions just because they are so much more flexible they would hardly notice the modes and aptitudes. At a first moment I thought we could expand Mesmerist powers and convert their Inspiration base into Psi, but maybe Aberrant rules, if used in the right way, could work really fine with Psiads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T15:09:17-08:00","id":1471040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1470917-let-s-talk-the-limits-of-nova-science?p=1471038#post1471038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your ideas. I honestly like the idea of Psiads working in a different way from Psions just because they are so much more flexible they would hardly notice the modes and aptitudes. At a first moment I thought we could expand Mesmerist powers and convert their Inspiration base into Psi, but maybe Aberrant rules, if used in the right way, could work really fine with Psiads.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, the main changes that I would make between Nova and Psiad would be a removal of transformations and transcendence on the one hand, had a replacement for the mega attribute prerequisites on the other. Shouldn't have or need mega attributes, just mega edges and in some cases quantum powers.<br /> <br /> But we're getting off topic, so I'll stop now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T15:33:01-08:00","id":1471042,"title":"","content":"I feel like dimensional travel would primarily be a Talent thing. Flux explicitly is the energy between worlds. I mean, I guess Nova's would be able to brute force a solution, but Talents would be much more efficient at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T15:49:01-08:00","id":1471043,"title":"","content":"uber-Talents, perhaps. The ones seen so far, whether they be the core book ones, the Adventure daredevils, or the alien ones, all deal know with things like luck than with Dimensional travel. So it's more of a \u201cthey <i>could</i> do dimensional travel, but they don't.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T16:36:48-08:00","id":1471049,"title":"","content":"In Media Res ( <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/272162/Trinity-Continuum-In-Media-Res?term=In+media+res\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...m=In+media+res</a> ) has a story about dimensional travel, and it really seams based in Talents, as the activation consumes Inspiration. Worth the reading, pages 28 to 37.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T17:10:16-08:00","id":1471055,"title":"","content":"Would that be the one about the Myst between worlds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T18:04:20-08:00","id":1471060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1470917-let-s-talk-the-limits-of-nova-science?p=1470923#post1470923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the list is not only doable, but it was done at some point before 2028.<br /> <br /> 1. N-Day is essentially this, but on global scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but what about something more controllable. Say a nova version of a prometheus chamber. Because what mad scientist doesn't want a way to empower his followers. (for that matter, a nova who wants to be richer than God could sell appointments).<br /> <br /> So let's go with a few versions to see what the probable difficulty would be. <br /> <br /> 1. A chamber that just triggers someone with the latent potential. <br /> <br /> 2. A chamber that can grant a baseline <i>without</i> such potential nova powers. (in the old players guide, I think this was expressed as a Qauntum 8 power).<br /> <br /> 3. a chamber that can allow either subject or operator some control over how their powers manifest, IE, letting someone chose to vocus on megaatributes or powers, and if powers, define what type.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T18:16:45-08:00","id":1471063,"title":"","content":"Option 2 isn't really all that amazing. And neither is option 3, if the Nova and his victim, err, subject, talk it out ahead of time. You can use the super science rule to implant powers of your choice in people, anyone. The catch is twofold: first, they are not Novas, and do not have the growth potential that novus have. They cannot max out their powers, and therefore cannot grow them. Nor can they gain new powers that they did not already have. However, they can develop transformations. And they tend to do so. They are basically the Nova era version of \u00c6on's sub-aberrants. <br /> <br /> The first option, triggering an Eruption, shouldn't be hard either. Just dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-21T19:29:33-08:00","id":1471064,"title":"","content":"Huh. odd my response vanished. I blame Backlash. <br /> <br /> For the other ones, I was thinking more a long the line of something Duplicating the old Quantum 8 power in Players guide, where no, you get honest to God, new novas, with everything that implies. So they can increase their quantum, develop new powers the whole thing. IE, if anyone's ever read Worm, a nova trying to pull off the Cauldron &quot;powers on demand.&quot; <br /> <br /> Needless to say, depending on where you want to go with it, it could come with &quot;fun&quot; issues in the &quot;Friend Computer and R&amp;D&quot; sense of fun. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-25T21:21:42-08:00","id":1471258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeonstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1470917-let-s-talk-the-limits-of-nova-science?p=1471029#post1471029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a sidenote I disliked the whole novas can't do telepathy etc so if a player can give me a good reason I allow them to have those powers. I liked the whole novas can do anything in 1E but have do deal taint so I just kept the concept for 2E, I view it as novas dealing with transcendence is the downside to having unlimited potential.<br /> <br /> Sorry for the mini rant, it's just my personal opinion which your free to disagree with it just seems that there a few random things that have been thrown into the rules just to nerf or be novas kryptonite.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I think most people that play Aberrant feel the same way. It's an arbitrary decision that looks &amp; feels like it was made purely to give people a reason to buy <b>Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on</b>. Not saying it was intended that way, but it's can certainly <b>feel</b> that way. Aberrant is a perfectly good system for playing a wide swathe of super-hero genre games - change the background (&amp; society paths), find a new explanation for Transcendence (not hard), then add in the missing powers of precognition, telepathy, &amp; clairvoyance and you could easily play anything from X-Men to Eternals.<br /> <br /> Hell, I'm doing exactly that just mixing Core &amp; Aberrant to play a campaign themed around the comic: The Boys.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T03:51:41-08:00","id":1471270,"title":"","content":"The Q6+ powers in 1e APG we\u2019re a mix of things that are perfectly doable in TC.<br /> <br /> Most of the powers are only other powers with scale. Some are just boring uses of the power to change a planet, basically a bunch of rules to do things narratively.<br /> <br /> Quantum Authority and Mastery are a bunch of random powers that were connected by \u201cQuantum\u201d. They are techniques with bizarre explanations of how they are connected, like Illusion that work on your quantum signature and your powers, remote perception with extra steps, bestowing powers to people, etc. Turning people into Novas is another thing that falls in the next group of powers (narrative powers and plot hooks left in the hands of players).<br /> <br /> The remaining powers are plot hooks that make no sense to give to the players, Cross time travel, Time Travel, Universe Creation and Plank Scale. If you really want your character to have this kind of power in my game, it\u2019s better you become the GM, because it\u2019s going to be really hard to GM on a player that can undo whatever the GM want to happen:<br /> GM: \u201cok, there is a neutron star coming to the general direction of Earth and it will eventually hit it. It is to big and heavy to be moved\u201d.<br /> Player of a Cross time Traveler: \u201cI take us to a universe where this star will not bother Earth\u201d.<br /> GM: \u201cWhat about the people you love in your universe?\u201d<br /> CTT: \u201cThey are in the new universe we moved into too, so we won\u2019t miss, also there are infinite universes where it will happen, saving one will not matter in the long run\u201d<br /> Anyway, these powers can be done by power stunt easily, because you are not going to do this kind of thing very often, at least not without taking the GM chair, so using it once in a while with a small chance of failing is not that big deal, and you are not going to spend XP in powers that you won\u2019t use very often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}